  A native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so the on/off state and the click-the-text-to-toggle behavior
  come from the browser — no JS needed. The page has no CSS, JS, or test setup, so there was nothing to run against it.

  One thing worth noting: this is a single standalone checkbox, since the page has no task list or items to attach one
  to yet. If you meant a checkbox per task item once a list exists, that's a different shape (rendering, per-item state,
  persistence) — say the word and we can work through it.

